umber, the order is from highest to lowest place value. So the final number would be:\n\n5 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 7 (ones). So putting it all together: 563,937,807?\n\nWait, let me check again step by step. Maybe I made a mistake in the positions.\n\nLet me do the addition step by step again more carefully.\n\nLet me write both numbers aligned properly:\n\n       2 8 2 9 1 1 0 5 9\n     + 2 8 1 0 2 6 7 4 8\n     --------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes: 9 + 8 = 17. Write down 7, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 5 + 4 = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 0 +7 =7 +1 =8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nThousands: 1 +6 =7. Write 7.\n\nTen thousands: 1 +2 =3. Write 3.\n\nHundred thousands: 9 +0 =9. Write 9.\n\nMillions: 2 +1 =3. Write 3.\n\nTen millions:8 +8 =16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nHundred millions:2 +2 =4 +1 (carry) =5. Write 5.\n\nSo the result is 5 6 3 9 3 7 8 0 7. So 563,937,807.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method. Maybe using calculator-like addition.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n282,911,059\n\n+281,026,748\n\nLet me add the millions:\n\n282,911,059 is 282 million plus 911,059.\n\n281,026,748 is 281 million plus 26,748.\n\nAdding the millions: 282 +281 = 563 million.\n\nNow adding the remaining parts: 911,059 +26,748.\n\n911,059 +26,748:\n\nAdding those:\n\n911,059\n\n+ 26,748\n\n= 911,059 +20,000 = 931,059; then +6,748 = 937,807.\n\nSo total is 563,000,000 + 937,807 = 563,937,807. That matches the previous result.\n\nSo the answer should be 563,937,807. Let me just confirm once more.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check by estimating:\n\n282 million plus 281 million is about 563 million, which aligns. The smaller parts add up to about 937k, so total is 563,937,807. Looks correct.\n\nTherefore, the final sum is 563,937,807.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 282911059 and 281026748?  .\n