5\n\nBreaking down similarly:\n\n5 (hundred millions place?), 7 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nWait let's confirm:\n\n500,000,000 +70,000,000 +9,000,000 +300,000 +10,000 +4,000 +600 +10 +5 = 579,314,615. Correct.\n\nSo now, aligning both numbers by their digits:\n\nFirst number (833,931,691):\n\nHundred millions:8\n\nTen millions:3\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:9\n\nOnes:1\n\nSecond number (579,314,615):\n\nHundred millions:5\n\nTen millions:7\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:1\n\nOnes:5\n\nWait, but when adding, we need to add each corresponding place. Let's start from the ones place and move left, keeping track of carries.\n\nStarting with Ones place:\n\n1 (from first) +5 (second) =6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nTens place:9 +1=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:6 (first) +6 (second)=12 +1 (carry)=13. Write 3, carryover1.\n\nThousands place:1 (first) +4 (second)=5 +1 (carry)=6. Write6, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:3 (first) +1 (second)=4. Write4.\n\nHundred thousands place:9 (first) +3 (second)=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nMillions place:3 (first) +9 (second)=12 +1 (carry)=13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nTen millions place:3 (first) +7 (second)=10 +1 (carry)=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions place:8 (first) +5 (second)=13 +1 (carry)=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, we add the final carryover 1 as a new digit on the left.\n\nSo putting it all together from right to left:\n\nOnes:6\n\nTens:0\n\nHundreds:3\n\nThousands:6\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nMillions:3\n\nTen millions:1\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nPlus the final carryover 1 in the billions place.\n\nSo the total sum is 1,413,246,306.\n\nWait let me check again step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:1+5=6 ✔️\n\nTens:9+1=10 →0,